  "chapter": 565,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 29 Chapter 565\n \n         MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 671, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the banking law, in relation to modifying delin-\n        quent home loans and single point of contact\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require a mortgage lender to provide a borrower who is\n60 days delinquent on his or her  home  loan  and  who  pursues  a  loan\nmodification or other foreclosure prevention alternative, a single point\nof  contact  for  the  borrower to reach the lender regarding pursuing a\nloan modification. I agree with the intent of the bill, and the  Depart-\nment  of  Financial  Services  has  already  implemented  regulations to\nrequire this process to assist consumers. To ensure a lender  identifies\na point of contact for a borrower in an efficient manner, I have reached\nagreement  with  the  Legislature  on a technical modification to ensure\nsuch contact is appointed when a borrower is 30 days late,  rather  than\n60, consistent with the regulation.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
